+# Volt kit door and fender fit — 3 November 2026
+
+The owner rejected the previous body-kit pass: skirts covered the door bottoms and all four approaches to the wheel openings left exposed gaps. This correction lowers all fifteen skirts below the doors and fits both skirt ends and all four bumper returns to the actual painted fender curves. It supersedes the previous refinement's appearance acceptance; its passing coverage counters did not establish correct door/fender fit.
+
+VDF01 keeps the whole skirt beneath the factory door-bottom datum of 0.31 in the reference model. Variant tops are now 0.281–0.298, replacing 0.355–0.455 including the former rear rise. VDF02 replaces fixed ±0.90 skirt ends and ±1.94 bumper ends with height-dependent points sampled from the existing fender openings. Each visible attachment is within 1.1 mm of that reference boundary, including the intentional 1 mm outward skin offset. These dimensions are in the existing unscaled model coordinates. VDF03 refreshes module/photo revision `volt-door-fender-fit-2` and the prepared representations. Original, item IDs, ownership, other kit categories and canonical handling remain.
+
+[Before and after](evidence/volt-door-fender-fit-2026-11-03/before-after.jpg) · [All fifteen corrected packages](evidence/volt-door-fender-fit-2026-11-03/all-body-kits.jpg) · [Native review](evidence/volt-door-fender-fit-2026-11-03/review.html)
+
+The shipping change is confined to `game/vehicle/electric_body_kits.gd`. New `arch_joint` points fit the existing painted openings, the skirts taper down between their fitted ends, and the complete bumper returns now reach the opposite sides of the same openings. The door-area sheet metal, its seams and livery are unchanged. `electric_kits.gd`, the customisation catalogue, modular loader and all 62 hood mesh files are byte exact against the preceding refinement checkpoint. The hood bank also validates the exact existing body and mesh builder hashes. Other concurrent build-identity and Garage-cache changes predate or are outside this correction and were preserved.
+
+| Check | Actual outcome |
+| --- | --- |
+| `test_volt_door_fender_fit.gd --headless` | 540 checks, zero failures, all fifteen options in both model qualities. Checks the actual mesh buffers against door height and factory fender attachment boundaries. |
+| Same fixture with `-- --fit-control` | 540 checks, 480 failures against the archived rejected geometry. |
+| `test_volt_body_construction.gd --headless` | 8,162 checks, zero failures; closed shells, coverage, finite normals, nondegenerate triangles and unchanged 30,000/9,000 body budgets. |
+| `test_volt_body_kit_wheel_fit.gd --headless` | 181 checks, zero failures. Existing 180 wheel/pose cases plus an intentional solid obstruction that must be detected. Tire hull queries retain a 2 mm margin. |
+| `test_volt_kits.gd --headless` | 610 checks, zero failures; category IDs, distinct shapes, independent changes and Original restoration. |
+| `test_modular_car_assets.gd --headless -- --vehicle=electric --all-kits` | 1,788 checks, zero failures; all 120 prepared modules, stock bases and race/ghost geometry agree with their source constructors. |
+| `test_volt_kits_garage.gd` | 54 checks, zero failures on each desktop renderer; preview, fixture save/reload/equip, purchase cancellation and actual race/ghost construction. |
+| Final native capture | 105 plain views plus 55 purple/red patterned views per desktop renderer: 320 final images. |
+| Matched native before/control capture | 105 current-room views of the archived rejected parts. All ten Original silver/blue control views have exactly zero changed RGB pixels against the final capture. |
+| Native visibility comparisons | All 75 silver option/angle pairs exceed the existing 1,500-pixel visibility threshold; minimum 10,284 pixels with an RGB-channel difference greater than 12. This measures visibility, not appearance acceptance. |
+
+The old rectangular tire-bounds test reported 117 failures once the skirts and corners were correctly extended to the curved fenders. Bounds now remain the broad rejection step; overlapping bounds proceed to actual convex tire-hull versus kit-triangle collision queries. This removes rectangular empty-space false positives while retaining real clearance assertions. The positive obstruction check verifies that a disabled or empty physics world cannot silently pass the fixture.
+
+The former construction test also demanded sill coverage at height 0.34, above the factory door bottoms. That incorrect coverage sample is replaced with 0.25/0.265/0.28 inside the corrected lower skirt; complete bumper and corner coverage, shell topology and geometry budgets remain. New independent door/fender tests reject the previously accepted parts rather than merely accepting the revised sampling window.
+
+All engine launches use pinned Godot 4.7.2 through `scripts/run_no_crash_dialog.py`, isolated task APPDATA/LOCALAPPDATA and empty BMT_API_URL. Reproduce with `python scripts/run_volt_fit.py <log-name> res://tests/<script>.gd <engine flags> -- <script flags>`. Each evidence log begins with its exact command and records exit status. The wrapper rejects other engine/script errors; Windows' existing certificate-store read error is retained. `run_volt_fit.py` now uses its own profile/evidence directories, and construction runs support an explicit report destination. `volt_body_review.ps1 -EvidencePath docs/evidence/volt-door-fender-fit-2026-11-03` builds the review from actual native images without additional packages.
+
+Four Volt bases, 120 full/simple modules and the Volt Garage rest scene are rebuilt from the final source. The preceding 105 Compatibility captures are retained separately in `previous-recording`; shared Garage/build context differs from that earlier recording. A new `--body-control` capture renders the archived rejected body parts inside the current isolated showroom to provide matched lighting/camera comparisons. Plain silver/blue views and purple/red patterned liveries are reviewed under both desktop renderers. The evidence completion receipt links the accepted logs.
+
+Initial fit checks caught a rear flank-offset applied twice and a small factory-tip height correction; those were fixed in the geometry. Construction checks then found coincident bottom rows where an extended bumper blade converged on the arch foot. The final attachment starts 3 mm above the datum and preserves a monotone section, retaining all edge-pairing and triangle tests. A full intermediate module bake was superseded and rebuilt completely. The sandbox denied attempts to stop the exact Codex-owned superseded test process trees, so the bounded runners finished normally; no owner process was targeted. Initial failures, intermediate captures and the final results are retained separately.
+
+The evidence includes scoped before/final snapshots, source preservation checks and a binary-inclusive task-only checkpoint with forward/reverse content checks. The main Git index is untouched. No device query/test, APK, owner save/process change, real purchase, live/backend mutation or deployment was performed. Reload is required for the new module/photo revision. Owner appearance and physical-device performance acceptance remain.
